Finally, we do LFI bruteforcing with lfi-linux.list (/etc/apache2/site-enabled)

The directory /etc/apache2/sites-enabled typically contains symbolic links to configuration files located in the /etc/apache2/sites-available directory. These configuration files define virtual hosts or websites that Apache HTTP Server can serve.

it displays in view-source:
---------------------------

<VirtualHost *:80>
	ServerAdmin webmaster@localhost
	ServerName broadcast.vulnnet.thm
	DocumentRoot /var/www/html
	ErrorLog ${APACHE_LOG_DIR}/error.log
	CustomLog ${APACHE_LOG_DIR}/access.log combined
	<Directory /var/www/html>
		Order allow,deny
		allow from all
		AuthType Basic
		AuthName "Restricted Content"
		AuthUserFile /etc/apache2/.htpasswd
		Require valid-user


